cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this paper or its Lean formalization, please cite it as below.
  Cite OpenAI's circulant Hadamard formalization separately when using the
  upstream files listed in UPSTREAM.md.
type: software
title: 'Group-invariant Butson Hadamard matrices: a prime dividing the order exactly once'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-09'
authors:
  - name: '[AUTHOR NAME]'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A paper and Lean 4 formalization showing that if a prime p divides the
  order of a finite abelian group G exactly once and is unramified in
  Q(zeta_h), there is no G-invariant Butson Hadamard matrix BH(G,h)
  (equivalently no generalized bent function G -> Z_h, and no perfect
  sequence of length |G| over the h-th roots of unity for cyclic G). It
  includes a corollary on semi-regular relative difference sets, Do Duc's
  condition (ii), and, for the ramified family BH(pq^e,p), a comparison lemma
  at the ramified prime (Lemma A) and nonexistence for all primes p != q and
  e >= 1 (Theorem C). The results were found, verified and formalized by
  Claude (Anthropic) agents under the repository owner's direction. Lean
  checks the stated theorems with axioms propext, Classical.choice and
  Quot.sound only. No human peer review has taken place, and the prior-art
  check against several paywalled references is pending; no
  historical-priority claim is made.
keywords:
  - Butson Hadamard matrix
  - perfect sequence
  - generalized bent function
  - relative difference set
  - cyclotomic integers
  - Lean
  - formal verification
references:
  - type: software
    title: 'The circulant Hadamard conjecture (Lean formalization)'
    authors:
